  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1850 is titled Making Arrangements in Eastern Sea, and the range opens on the Shen clan headquarters.",
      "chapters": [
        1850
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_eastern_sea",
        "fac_shen_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chaos in Central Continent leaves two threads running into it. Fairy Zi Wei identifies the dragonman blessed land as belonging to Duke Long’s grandson Wu Shuai and treats it as holding clues toward Immortal Gu House Dragon Palace, one of whose creators was Wu Shuai; Heavenly Court had been searching for Dragon Palace with little progress, and with this clue she expects they can deduce its location. Qin Ding Ling judges that Dragon Palace’s exposure means Fang Yuan is already racing for it, so Fairy Zi Wei returns to Heavenly Court to run deductions. Qin Ding Ling also finds Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s hidden path into Heavenly Court, and Fairy Zi Wei treats the find as leverage for an ambush on Northern Plains ahead of the Central Continent Refinement Path Convention.",
      "chapters": [
        1831
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "evt_arc_central_continent_chaos",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei",
        "char_duke_long",
        "char_wu_shuai",
        "sys_immortal_gu_house",
        "house_dragon_palace",
        "fac_heavenly_court",
        "char_qin_ding_ling",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_giant_sun_immortal_venerable",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "sys_refinement_path_convention"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s pressure on Eastern Sea’s Shen Cong Sheng and the five regions chaotic war talk tied to fate Gu repair.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-region-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_shen_cong_sheng",
        "gu_fate_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan presses Eastern Sea’s Shen Cong Sheng while both sides already foresee a five regions chaotic war that will overturn existing order. In that talk, Heavenly Court must repair fate Gu, and Fang Yuan needs large amounts of low ranked immortal materials to strike at Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [
        1910
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "five-region-pressure",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "The four Central Continent battlefields and Longevity Heaven’s disadvantage inside Heavenly Court.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-court-war",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "reg_central_continent",
        "fac_longevity_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan maps four main battlefields: Infallible blessed land, Hidden Dragon Cave, Emperor City, and Heavenly Court. He names Heavenly Court’s battlefield the decisive one because fate Gu is there, and winning means destroying it. Longevity Heaven is already at a disadvantage inside Heavenly Court after Heavenly Court uses Qin Ding Ling’s discovery of Giant Sun Immortal Venerable’s arrangement to ambush them instead.",
      "chapters": [
        1928
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "heavenly-court-war",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_infallible_blessed_land",
        "loc_hidden_dragon_cave",
        "loc_emperor_city"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Duke Long’s hit that drops Fang Yuan before Embroidered Tower, and Reckless Savage Demon Venerable’s blood skins there.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "embroidered-tower",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_embroidered_tower",
        "char_reckless_savage_demon_venerable"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan suffers Duke Long’s attack and collapses in his own blood in front of Embroidered Tower. Three blood skins of Reckless Savage Demon Venerable are sewn in the air above it; blown by the battlefield winds, they loosen and wave like banners.",
      "chapters": [
        1953
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "embroidered-tower",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan reaches fate Gu at Heaven Overseeing Tower and crushes it.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "destroying-fate-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_heaven_overseeing_tower"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1960 is titled Destroying Fate. Fang Yuan reaches fate Gu at the top of Heaven Overseeing Tower, grabs the rank nine Gu, and crushes it into pieces.",
      "chapters": [
        1960
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "destroying-fate-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1961 is titled So What If It Was Destroyed and opens at the moment fate Gu is destroyed.",
      "chapters": [
        1961
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "destroying-fate-gu",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Red Lotus’ gift to Feng Jiu Ge on stone lotus island, and chapter 1965’s retelling of the Embroidered Tower hit.",
      "chapters": [],
      "certainty": "inferred",
      "confidence": "C",
      "verification": "no_citation",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feng-jiu-ge-and-reckless-savage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Chapter 1965 is titled He Was Still Feng Jiu Ge. On stone lotus island, Red Lotus’ will gives Feng Jiu Ge future self and an incomplete destiny Gu recipe, while reminding him that destiny song stays sealed while fate Gu still exists. Feng Jiu Ge refuses to destroy Fate or resist Heavenly Court for that gift alone. On the battlefield, after Fang Yuan transmits to him, Feng Jiu Ge replies secretly that everything still depends on you. Chapter 1965 retells that Fang Yuan purposely took Duke Long’s hit toward Embroidered Tower and activated Reckless Savage Demon Venerable’s hidden arrangement, using that strength against fate Gu.",
      "chapters": [
        1965
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "feng-jiu-ge-and-reckless-savage",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_feng_jiu_ge",
        "gu_destiny_gu",
        "char_fang_yuan"
      ]
    }
  ],
